sgi-l1-usb-control (0.1.51) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Updated components since 0.1.50: user-space sgil1ctl only; kernel module
    source is unchanged.
  * Suppress the redundant raw L1 debug line in top-level sgil1ctl debug
    output while retaining the decoded virtual-switch report.
  * Make debug and power command help shorter and more consistent, using
    switch terminology and leaving hidden aliases undocumented.
  * Make set-date the documented date-setting shortcut and hide date/wait
    option aliases from help while keeping them accepted.
  * Support power down --follow and wait --power-down --follow LED diagnostics.
  * Allow high-level power down to send one power-down signal without --force,
    while --force sends the second SGI power-down signal immediately.
  * Buffer early power up/down LED-follow samples until power-state
    confirmation or a short timeout, and reuse discovered command routes where
    possible during follow hand-off.
  * Reduce LED-follow recovery backoff so transient USB recovery does not
    suppress boot diagnostics for multiple seconds.

 -- Stuart Shelton <stuart@shelton.me>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 13:18:29 +0100

sgi-l1-usb-control (0.1.50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Updated components since 0.1.49: user-space sgil1ctl only; kernel module
    source is unchanged.
  * Add command-specific sgil1ctl COMMAND --help output for option-bearing
    commands and low-level helpers.
  * Allow sgil1ctl power up without --force while continuing to accept --force
    for compatibility.
  * Add sgil1ctl debug to decode documented virtual debug switches, show l1dbg
    state, and guarded update helpers for named virtual debug switch fields.
  * Rename the documented debug switch listing option to --list-switches,
    with --list as a short alias.
  * Remove the undocumented debug --list-features alias.
  * Enter LED-follow immediately after power up --follow and
    wait --power-up --follow, then report power-check confirmation once it
    succeeds during follow.
  * Accept logs as a hidden compatibility alias for log.

